---
import Container from "@components/Container.astro";
import PageLayout from "@layouts/PageLayout.astro";

const UPDATED = "13 November 2026";
const EMAIL = "atulpatare99@gmail.com";
---

<PageLayout
  title="FormFit Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy policy for FormFit, the offline photo and signature resizer. FormFit collects no data."
>
  <Container>
    <div class="animate text-center mt-10 mb-10">
      <div class="text-4xl font-semibold text-black dark:text-white">
        FormFit Privacy Policy
      </div>
      <div class="mt-3 text-xs text-muted-foreground">Last updated: {UPDATED}</div>
    </div>

    <article class="animate">
      <p>
        FormFit ("the app"), developed by <strong>Atul Patare</strong>, is a photo and signature
        resizer, compressor and converter for exam and government forms. This policy explains how
        the app handles your information. In short: <strong>it doesn't collect any.</strong>
      </p>

      <h2>Summary</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>No data collection.</strong> FormFit does not collect, store on any server,
          transmit, share or sell any personal information, images or usage data.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Fully offline.</strong> The app does not request the Internet permission, so it
          cannot send anything off your device.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>No ads, no analytics, no crash reporting, no tracking, no third-party SDKs, no
          account or login.</strong>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Images you select</h2>
      <p>
        Images you choose through the system photo picker, the file picker, or the Android "Share"
        menu are read only to resize, compress or convert them <strong>on your device</strong>. The
        app never uploads them.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Temporary output files are kept in the app's private cache and deleted when you clear
          results or start a new batch.
        </li>
        <li>Files you choose to <strong>Save</strong> are written to <code>Pictures/FormFit</code> on your device.</li>
        <li>
          Files you choose to <strong>Share</strong> are handed to the app you pick, under that
          app's own privacy policy.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Permissions</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Photo picker / file picker:</strong> gives the app access only to the images you
          choose, never your whole gallery.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Storage (Android 8 and 9 only):</strong> needed to save output to your Pictures
          folder on older Android versions. It is not requested on Android 10 and above.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Settings</h2>
      <p>
        Your last used size settings and language are stored locally on your device so they are
        remembered next time. They are never sent anywhere and are removed when you uninstall the
        app or clear its data.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        The app does not collect any information from anyone, including children under 13.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        If this policy changes, the updated version will be published at this same address with a
        new "Last updated" date.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions or concerns about this policy: <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a>
      </p>
    </article>
  </Container>
</PageLayout>
